<description>
Decode a stamp map: read templates, markers, and palette from a tiled grid, then render stamps.

Input structure:
- Grid divided into K tile columns (each N wide) separated by 1-col dashed separators.
- Top band (rows 0..N-1): K template masks, one per tile column.
- Middle band (rows N+1..2N): marker pixels whose color picks a template.
- Bottom band (rows 2N+2..): K palette swatches giving the output color per template.
- Separator rows at rows N and 2N+1 (dashed pattern of sep color).

Rule:
- Each marker's local position (lr, lc) within its tile column determines which N×N output block to stamp.
- The marker's color identifies which template to use; the palette recolors the template.

Key insight: Marker color encodes template index; local position within tile column encodes stamp block.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "template-color marker pixels s in the middle band (between top templates and bottom palette)",
  "dst": "stamp slots d in an N×N grid of N×N tiles",
  "match_cond": "s.color == template_color[j]; d.pos == (s.r mod N, s.c mod N)",
  "transform": "replace d with template_mask[j] recolored to palette_color[j] (palette read from bottom band, left→right aligned to template columns)"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task_type: move_to_match (decode stamp map)
  grid:
    H: 2N+2 + pal_h rows (+ 0-2 trailing bg pad rows [observed])
    W: K*N + (K-1) cols (+ 0-7 trailing bg pad cols [observed])
    N (tile size): 3-5
    K (num templates): 3-4
    pal_h: 2 typical, up to 4 [observed]
  colors:
    bg: most common color (0 in all [observed])
    sep: 5 in all [observed]; second most common; forms thick dashed separators
    template_colors: K distinct non-bg non-sep colors
    palette_colors: K non-bg non-sep colors; may overlap with template_colors
  bands (vertical, top-to-bottom):
    top_band: rows 0..N-1 — K templates, each N x N, with 1-col gap separating them
    thick_sep_row: row N — dashed sep line (see pattern below)
    middle_band: rows N+1..2N — marker pixels (N rows)
    thick_sep_row2: row 2N+1 — dashed sep line
    bottom_band: rows 2N+2..H-1 — K palette swatches
  thick_sep_pattern: |
    dashed: at sep row r, col c gets sep iff (c mod (N+1)) is even, else bg.
    Equivalently: sep at cols 0,2,4,...,N-1 within each tile + at inter-tile sep cols.
    Same pattern on thick sep cols (vertical).
  templates:
    shape: N x N binary mask of template_color on bg
    connectivity: 8-connected single component [observed]
    density: 50-100% of N*N cells [observed]
    symmetry: mixed; some LR/UD symmetric, some not [observed]
  palette_swatch:
    shape: 1-2 pixels of palette_color at center-ish of its N-wide column, in the last row of pal_h
    j-th swatch recolors j-th template (aligned by column position)
  markers:
    middle-band cells (compressed, excluding thick sep cols) contain marker pixels
    color = one of the K template_colors
    count: total 60-100% of N*N cells across all templates; 0-100% per template
    disjoint: different template markers occupy disjoint (r mod N, c mod N) slots
    tile_column_uniform: each tile column in the middle band contains markers of exactly one template color; there is a 1-to-1 mapping from templates to tile columns (not necessarily identity)
    placement: arbitrary within middle band (not required to match template shape)
  output:
    shape: (N*N) x (N*N)
    construction: for each marker at (r,c) colored c_j (template j), paint template_mask[j] recolored to palette[j] at output block (r%N * N, c%N * N)

generation_strategy: |
  Output-first, then invert. Build the stamp decisions, then place markers.
  1. Sample N in 3-5, K in 3-4; choose bg=0, sep=5.
  2. Pick K distinct template colors and K palette colors (both subsets of 1-9 minus bg,sep; palette may reuse template colors).
  3. For each template j: sample an N x N binary mask (single 8-connected component, density 50-100%, include some symmetric and some not).
  4. Assign stamp placements: for each of the N*N slots (rr,cc), randomly pick one template index (or leave empty with small prob, target ~75-90% slot coverage). Ensures disjoint per-template slot sets.
  5. Assign a random 1-to-1 mapping from templates to tile columns. For each (j, slot) assignment, place marker of color tcols[j] at row r in [N+1, 2N] where (r-(N+1)) % N == rr, in the tile column assigned to template j at local column cc.
  6. Build the full input grid:
     - Place K templates in top band (row 0..N-1), separated by 1-col sep gaps.
     - Stamp dashed thick_sep rows at row N and 2N+1, thick_sep cols at N, 2N+1, ..., using the dashed pattern (sep at even positions within each tile, bg at odd).
     - Write markers into the middle band cells chosen in step 5.
     - Put palette swatches in bottom band: one palette_color pixel (or small cluster) roughly centered in each tile column.
     - Optionally pad with trailing bg rows/cols (0-2 rows, 0-7 cols).
  7. Run the solver on the constructed input and assert the output matches the constructed stamp-map rendering.
```
</generation_spec>
